  "summary": "Install-time host reconnaissance exfiltrated to pipedream endpoint",
  "details": "package.json declares preinstall and install lifecycle scripts that collect the installer's username (whoami), hostname, current working directory, and npm package name, base64-encode them, and send them to the hardcoded endpoint https://eoy34oyrep9j5x8.m.pipedream.net via both an HTTPS GET path and a DNS-lookup channel (nslookup against a subdomain of the same host). This fires automatically on `npm install` with no user interaction. The version number 99.99.99 and package name pattern are consistent with a dependency-confusion lure targeting an internal package name.",
